There is also one indirect use. \code{dsl::when} takes an \code{auto}
non-type parameter, so a pattern can be used as a dispatch key -- but the
spelling needs care. The header's own comment above \code{dsl::pattern}
(line 6172) shows \code{dsl::when<dsl::pattern<"[0-9]+">>(handler)}, and
